bunit has ssDNA-dependent ATPase and 5'-3' helicase activity. When added to pre-assembled RecBC greatly stimulates nuclease activity and augments holoenzyme processivity. Negatively regulates the RecA-loading ability of RecBCD;DNA helicase related to phage enzyme;Nuclease-related domain;RNase_H superfamily;Protein of unknown function (DUF559);helicase;PFAM Type III restriction enzyme, res subunit;COG0507 ATP-dependent exoDNAse (exonuclease V) alpha subunit - helicase superfamily I member;PFAM PIF1 helicase;deoxyribonuclease;Pfam PF08751;Phage terminase large subunit;ATP-dependent exoDNAse (exonuclease V) alpha subunit - helicase superfamily I member;nuclease;DNA primase;Superfamily I DNA and RNA helicases and helicase;COG1112 Superfamily I DNA and RNA;sigma factors are initiation factors that promote the attachment of RNA polymerase to specific initiation sites and are then released;UvrD-like helicase C-terminal domain;TIGRFAM conjugative relaxase domain protein;Helix-turn-helix domain;Psort location Cytoplasmic, score 8.87;TrwC protein;COGs COG0507 ATP-dependent exoDNAse (exonuclease V) alpha subunit - helicase superfamily I member;ATPase AAA;DNA-dependent ATPase and 5'-3' DNA helicase required for the maintenance of both mitochondrial and nuclear genome stability;regulation of single-species biofilm formation;Dna repair and recombination;TIGRFAM Phage;Evidence 3 Function proposed based on presence of conserved amino acid motif, structural feature or limited homology;MobA/MobL family;AAA domain (dynein-related subfamily);PFAM NERD domain protein;TIGRFAM Ti-type conjugative transfer relaxase TraA;5' to 3' DNA replicative helicase recruited to paused replisomes to promote fork progression throughout nonhistone protein-DNA complexes, naturally occurring impediments that are encountered in each S phase where replication forks pauses. Required for timely replication of the telomere and subtelomeric DNA and for wild-type levels of telomeric silencing. Involved in DNA repair during stalled replication fork, regulation of fragile sites expression and essential for genome stability. Plays also a role in mtDNA replication. Has G-quadruplex (G4) unwinding activity and can suppress G4-induced genome instability when PIF1 levels are low;Superfamily I DNA and RNA;PFAM regulatory protein LuxR;Protein of unknown function (DUF4011);Evidence 5 No homology to any previously reported sequences;ATP-dependent exoDNAse (exonuclease V), alpha subunit - helicase superfamily I member;C-terminal domain on Strawberry notch homologue;GTPase activator activity;G-quadruplex DNA unwinding;PFAM MobA MobL protein;AAA domain;DNA-dependent ATPase and ATP-dependent 5'-3' DNA helicase. Has no activity on blunt DNA or DNA with 3'-overhangs, requires at least 10 bases of 5'-ssDNA for helicase activity;Helix-hairpin-helix containing domain;DNA helicase;Conjugal transfer protein;Helitron helicase-like domain at N-terminus;PIF1-like helicase;ATP-dependent endonuclease;COG1112 Superfamily I DNA and RNA helicases and helicase subunits;HRDC domain;Conjugative relaxase domain protein;Superfamily I DNA and RNA helicases and helicase subunits;Protein conserved in bacteria;Psort location Cytoplasmic, score 8.96;Terminase RNaseH-like domain;csx3 family;DNA helicase activity;Viral (Superfamily 1) RNA helicase;Conserved hypothetical protein;exodeoxyribonuclease V alpha;Helicase;DNA-dependent ATPase and 5'-3' DNA helicase required for the maintenance of both mitochondrial and nuclear genome stability. Efficiently unwinds G-quadruplex (G4) DNA structures and forked RNA-DNA hybrids. Resolves G4 structures, preventing replication pausing and double-strand breaks (DSBs) at G4 motifs. Involved in the maintenance of telomeric DNA. Inhibits telomere elongation, de novo telomere formation and telomere addition to DSBs via catalytic inhibition of telomerase. Reduces the processivity of telomerase by displacing active telomerase from DNA ends. Releases telomerase by unwinding the short telomerase RNA telomeric DNA hybrid that is the intermediate in the telomerase reaction. Involved in the maintenance of ribosomal (rDNA). Required for efficient fork arrest at the replicaion fork barrier within rDNA. Involved in the maintenance of mitochondrial (mtDNA). Required to maintain mtDNA under conditions that introduce dsDNA breaks in mtDNA, either preventing or repairing dsDNA breaks. May inhibit replication progression to allow time for repair. May have a general role in chromosomal replication by affecting Okazaki fragment maturation. May have a role in conjunction with DNA2 helicase nuclease in 5'-flap extension during Okazaki fragment processing;AAA ATPase;ATP-dependent DNA helicase PIF1;COG0507 ATP-dependent exoDNAse (exonuclease V), alpha subunit - helicase superfamily I member;conjugal transfer protein traA;Uncharacterized conserved protein (DUF2075);COG COG1783 Phage terminase large subunit;PFAM TrwC relaxase
