burst size and delays, but does not completely prevent lysis. Mutations in the muralytic domain of gene 16, an inner capsid protein, can partially compensate for a deletion of gp3.5. Other names gp3.5;Domain first found in C1r, C1s, uEGF, and bone morphogenetic protein.;chitinase;Alpha-glucosidase;Metallo-peptidase family M12;Glycosyl-hydrolase 97 N-terminal;N-acetyl-anhydromuranmyl-L-alanine amidase;Glycosyl-hydrolase 97 C-terminal, oligomerisation;COG3023 Negative regulator of beta-lactamase expression;Protein of unknown function (DUF1343);positive regulation of growth;Sporulation related domain;N-acetylmuramyl L-alanine amydase;Glycoside hydrolase, family 19;Ami_2;N-acetylmuramyl-L-alanine amidase, negative regulator of AmpC, AmpD;Peptidoglycan-binding domain 1 protein;Cpl-7 lysozyme C-terminal domain protein;hydrolase, family 25;COG COG3023 Negative regulator of beta-lactamase expression;N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanine amidase, family 2;Involved in both cell wall peptidoglycans recycling and beta-lactamase induction. Specifically cleaves the amide bond between the lactyl group of N-acetylmuramic acid and the alpha- amino group of the L-alanine in degradation products containing an anhydro N-acetylmuramyl moiety (By similarity);LGFP repeat;N-acetyl-anhydromuramoyl-L-alanine amidase activity;Psort location Cytoplasmic, score 8.96;isomerase activity;PFAM Glycoside hydrolase 97;PFAM N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanine amidase, family 2;lysozyme activity;PFAM N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanine amidase family 2;Negative regulator of beta-lactamase expression;N-Acetylmuramoyl-L-alanine amidase;SPTR N-acetylmuramyl-L-alanine amidase, negative regulator of AmpC, AmpD
